{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/init(uintValue:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/uintValue"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/Comparable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/Hashable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/UIntRepresentable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When polyphonic parts are involved, the ordering within a MusicXML document can differ from musical score"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. As an example, say we have a piano part in 4\/4 where within a single measure, all the notes on the top"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staff are followed by all the notes on the bottom staff. In this example, each staff has a slur that starts on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beat 2 and stops on beat 3, and there is a third slur that goes from beat 1 of one staff to beat 4 of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other staff."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this situation, the two mid-measure slurs can use the same number because they do not overlap in MusicXML"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document order, even though they do overlap in musical score order. Within the MusicXML document, the top"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staff slur will both start and stop before the bottom staff slur starts and stops."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the cross-staff slur starts in the top staff and stops in the bottom staff, it will need a separate number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the mid-measure slurs because it overlaps those slurs in MusicXML document order. However, if the cross-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staff slur starts in the bottom staff and stops in the top staff, all three slurs can use the same number."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"None of them overlap within the MusicXML document, even though they all overlap each other in the musical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"score order. Within the MusicXML document, the start and stop of the top-staff slur will be followed by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stop and start of the cross-staff slur, followed by the start and stop of the bottom-staff slur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As this example demonstrates, a reading program should be prepared to handle cases where the number-levels"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start and stop in an arbitrary order. Because the start and stop values refer to musical score order, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"program may find the stopping point of an object earlier in the MusicXML document than it will find its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starting point."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/Se","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SE","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s27ExpressibleByIntegerLiteralP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/10XestiTools17UIntRepresentableP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/SL":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SL","title":"Swift.Comparable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel/Hashable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","title":"Hashable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel\/hashable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/Hashable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[]},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype"},"doc://IvorMXL/s27ExpressibleByIntegerLiteralP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.ExpressibleByIntegerLiteral","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s27ExpressibleByIntegerLiteralP"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLNumberLevel"},"doc://IvorMXL/Se":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Decodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/Se"},"doc://IvorMXL/10XestiTools17UIntRepresentableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"XestiTools.UIntRepresentable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/10XestiTools17UIntRepresentableP"},"doc://IvorMXL/SE":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SE","title":"Swift.Encodable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel/UIntRepresentable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","title":"UIntRepresentable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel\/uintrepresentable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/UIntRepresentable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel/Equatable-Implementations":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/Equatable-Implementations","title":"Equatable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel\/equatable-implementations","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","abstract":[]},"doc://IvorMXL/s23CustomStringConvertibleP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","title":"Swift.CustomStringConvertible"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel/uintValue":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel\/uintValue","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in MusicXML document"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"uintValue","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel\/uintvalue","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"uintValue","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"